    "turn_text": "I absolutely believe that. First of all, I think women come to politics to solve problems. And aren't as enamored with, well, let's have a big debate, somebody wins, somebody loses, and we all get to go home and do this again next year. We don't have time for that. We got to get home and take care of our kids and our families. And we really come to solve problems. So I think we are better collaborators. I'm talking about today maybe 50 years from now it could be different. But I think women in politics tend to listen, find solutions, and then work to get that done. And I've seen it many times.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
