  {
    "episode_id": 90466,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90466.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 210,
    "turn_text": "It is not fashionable, but it is needed. It needs to be respected. We are a democracy. We are a country of a lot of different ideas. No one gets their way a hundred percent of the time. But if you keep in mind that the goal is to make things better, not to make it perfect, that's what has sustained us as a democracy for a very long time. And that's my job as a senator is to sustain that movement forward, fight for what I believe in, but at the end of the day, try and make it just a little better.",
