        "text": "The Republicans moved forward on repealing Obamacare in a specific manner.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "True tax reform should benefit middle-class families whose wages have stagnated for decades.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "A Republican budget proposal excludes Democrats from the decision-making process.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Tax reform should not be used as a cover for tax cuts benefiting the wealthiest Americans.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Excluding half the Senate from the conversation will make it difficult to secure enough votes.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Trickle-down economics does not reliably improve living conditions for struggling families.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Excluding Democrats will reduce public support for the Republican agenda.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "If Republicans express willingness to include Democrats, meaningful dialogue could occur.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The legitimacy of policy decisions depends on inclusive legislative processes.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Public trust in legislation correlates with broad political participation and transparency.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Middle-class families deserve economic policies that address wage stagnation.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Tax policy should prioritize equitable growth over concentrated wealth accumulation.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The term 'tax reform' has become a rhetorical tool masking regressive outcomes.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "Democratic input increases the likelihood of viable, bipartisan legislation.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "Republicans’ past actions suggest a pattern of exclusionary policymaking.",
